  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="4211-3361-6341-b746" name="Samurai (Armies of Antiquity) - List Notes" publicationId="aab0-aa1e-0319-4ffe" hidden="false">
      <description>SAMURAI ARMY LIST (Armies of Antiquity, pp.44-45), Japan c. AD 400-1250.
Designer's Note: the Samurai list is whimsical; serious players may want to tone down or leave out the Samurai heroes, warrior monks and peasants.
Characters: the army must have a General (not enforced) and may have up to a quarter of its points in Hero characters including the General. Samurai up to half the points; Infantry up to three quarters.
Warriors of Legend: Generals and Heroes may re-roll one failed to-hit and one failed to-wound roll in each combat phase, and may re-roll a failed armour save if the wound is their last one remaining.
Honourable: Samurai characters in a position to charge an enemy character must do so, and must accept a challenge issued by an enemy character (if several are eligible, any one may be chosen). Infantry units may not declare a charge until after a Samurai unit has declared a charge or fought a round of combat as a defender (they may declare in the same turn, after the Samurai).
Katana: a character or Samurai with a katana counts as having a shield as well (it can parry), and the katana adds +1 Strength on foot (mounted Samurai only use one hand, no bonus). With an additional hand weapon he loses the +1 Strength bonus but may still parry. Samurai Armour: 5+ armour save, counts as light armour for movement. Naginata: treated as a halberd on foot and a thrusting spear if mounted. Sashimono: any Samurai or Ashigaru unit may have them for +15 pts per unit; may re-roll a failed Break test. Bows: Samurai count as having a longbow, infantry have ordinary bows.

ARMY COMPOSITION (percentages by points):
  Characters: up to 25%
  Samurai: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 75%</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
